    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map policy1 permit 10', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'route-map policy1 permit 10', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco IOS configuration for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map policy1 permit 10\\n match protocol bgp\\n set ip next-hop self\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper `policy-statement policy1 term 1` translates to Cisco's `route-map policy1 permit 10`\\n- `from protocol bgp` becomes `match protocol bgp`\\n- `then next-hop self` becomes `set ip next-hop self`\\n- The `then accept` is implied by the `permit` action in the route-map statement\", 'trans_template': 'route-map policy1 permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match protocol bgp', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'match protocol bgp', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco IOS configuration for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map policy1 permit 10\\n match protocol bgp\\n set ip next-hop self\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper `policy-statement policy1 term 1` translates to Cisco's `route-map policy1 permit 10`\\n- `from protocol bgp` becomes `match protocol bgp`\\n- `then next-hop self` becomes `set ip next-hop self`\\n- The `then accept` is implied by the `permit` action in the route-map statement\", 'trans_template': 'match protocol bgp'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set ip next-hop self', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set ip next-hop self', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco IOS configuration for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map policy1 permit 10\\n match protocol bgp\\n set ip next-hop self\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper `policy-statement policy1 term 1` translates to Cisco's `route-map policy1 permit 10`\\n- `from protocol bgp` becomes `match protocol bgp`\\n- `then next-hop self` becomes `set ip next-hop self`\\n- The `then accept` is implied by the `permit` action in the route-map statement\", 'trans_template': 'set ip next-hop self'}]]": 1,
    "['term [parameter2] from protocol [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map policy1 permit 10', 'parent_command': ['route-map policy1 permit 10'], 'root': 'route-map policy1 permit 10', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map policy1 permit 10\\n match protocol bgp\\n##\\n\\nThe Cisco `route-map` is the equivalent of Juniper's `policy-statement`, with `permit 10` serving a similar role to `term 1`. The `match protocol bgp` corresponds to the `from protocol bgp` condition in Juniper.\", 'trans_template': 'route-map policy1 permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match protocol bgp', 'parent_command': ['route-map policy1 permit 10'], 'root': 'route-map policy1 permit 10', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map policy1 permit 10\\n match protocol bgp\\n##\\n\\nThe Cisco `route-map` is the equivalent of Juniper's `policy-statement`, with `permit 10` serving a similar role to `term 1`. The `match protocol bgp` corresponds to the `from protocol bgp` condition in Juniper.\", 'trans_template': 'match protocol bgp'}]]": 1,
